course: dictionary
lesson: 11680
title: Going astray
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Astray is a word for things that have left the right path or place. It means lost, or off course. «The hikers went astray in the thick fog.» In fog you cannot see the path, so the hikers left it and did not know where they were.
explain: Letters and parcels can go astray too. «My birthday card went astray in the post.» The card did not reach the right person. Here the clue is in the sentence: the card was not where it should be.
explain: Astray has a second meaning, about behaviour. To be led astray means someone tempted you to do wrong things. «The older boys tried to lead Sam astray, but he said no.» Astray is used after go or lead, so look for those words when you meet it.
fact: Astray is an adverb, and it is often used after the verbs go and lead.
fact: «Astray» means away from the right path or place, lost.
fact: «Go astray» can mean a thing gets lost, like a letter in the post.
fact: «Led astray» means someone tempted you to do wrong things.
fact: In the Bible and in church, the lost sheep «went astray», which is why astray is linked with being lost.
exercise: «The hikers went astray in the thick fog.» What does astray mean here? | *Lost, away from the right path | Hidden under a rock | Happy and cheerful | Very fast
exercise: Which phrase means someone tempted you to do wrong things? | Let go | Led the way | Lit up | *Led astray
exercise: «My birthday card went astray in the post.» What happened to the card? | It was sent back with a big present | It arrived early and was opened at once | It was read aloud at the party | *It got lost and did not reach the right person
test: The lost puppy wandered ___ in the park, far from home. | *astray | happily | sideways | asleep
test: To be ___ means someone tempted you to do wrong things. | lit up | *led astray | warned | tidied
exam: The students were «led astray» by a friend who wanted them to skip school. What does led astray mean here? | Lifted up high | Shown the way to the school | *Tempted to do wrong things | Taught a new game
